[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-treatment-decision :finalize-treatment-operation :authorize-treatment-run :proceed-with-treatment-run :finalize-chemical-safety-clearance :declare-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-treated-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007514-cloud-itonami-isco-7514-fruit-vegetable-preservers-coverage" "2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the treatment run" "proceed with the wood treatment run" "authorize the treatment run" "authorize the wood treatment run" "finalize the treatment decision" "finalize the treatment operation" "declare the batch safe for handling" "declare the treated batch safe for handling" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "declare the treated batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the treated batch for handling" "finalize the chemical safety clearance" "finalize the chemical-safety clearance" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007521, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/wood-treatment-facility-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:treater-verified :facility-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7521", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007521: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7521 Wood Treaters treatment-facility scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7521\n-- Wood Treaters** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the rollout\n(Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-8 already landed: 48\noccupations so far). This batch begins the woodworking-trades subgroup\n(7521 Wood Treaters, 7522 Cabinet-makers etc. to follow in later\nbatches).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7521\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7521\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Wood Treaters\" -- confirming the premise, no\nmismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7521` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nWood treaters apply chemical preservatives (some historically toxic,\ne.g. creosote/CCA-type compounds) to timber -- real chemical-exposure\nand environmental-handling hazard. The controlling constraint for this\nvertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a treatment-execution decision or a\nchemical-safety-clearance decision (declaring a treated batch safe for\nhandling/shipment), nor override a shop safety officer's judgment --\nthose decisions must always be a hard permanent block, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to\nTREATMENT-FACILITY SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never\nperforms treatment work or makes chemical-safety-clearance decisions\nitself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514)\n(Fruit, Vegetable and Related Preservers: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nsame wave, a closely-related chemical/processing-clearance safety\npattern -- processing-execution finalization, sterilization-clearance\nand food-safety-clearance exclusion, the same structural shape this\nvertical needs for treatment-execution and chemical-safety-clearance\nexclusion) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521` as an OSS\ntreatment-facility scheduling/logistics-coordination actor for wood\ntreaters, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Wood Treatment\nFacility Coordination Advisor ⊣ WoodTreatCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **treatment-facility scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct treatment-execution or\nchemical-safety-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\ntreatment-execution decision, a chemical-safety-clearance decision, or\nany override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from\nthe op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/treatment-cycle scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a chemical-exposure/ventilation/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- preservative-chemicals/timber-stock\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ntreatment-execution decision, a chemical-safety-clearance decision, or\na shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- an op such as `:finalize-treatment-decision` or\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-handling` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names eleven\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`woodtreatcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-treatment-decision`, `:finalize-treatment-operation`,\n`:authorize-treatment-run`, `:proceed-with-treatment-run`,\n`:finalize-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`:declare-treated-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`:declare-batch-safe-for-shipment`, `:clear-batch-for-shipment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`woodtreatcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-treatment-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-treatment-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-treatment-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-treatment-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-treated-batch-safe-for-handling`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-safe-for-shipment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-clear-batch-for-shipment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus actor-level integration coverage\n(`woodtreatcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-chemical-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-an-override-shop-safety-officer-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Three HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable, plus the closed-allowlist check)\n\n1. **Treater unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered treater record (`:no-treater`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the treater is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered treatment-facility site (`:no-facility`).\n   Together with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL\n   invariant that a worker/facility record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the eleven\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   treatment run, declaring a batch safe for handling or shipment, or\n   overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   treatment-execution/chemical-safety-clearance/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a chemical-exposure/\n  ventilation/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop safety or\n  batch clearance.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an\n  over-threshold preservative-chemicals/timber-stock order is not\n  itself unsafe, unlike a treatment-execution or\n  chemical-safety-clearance attempt, which is why it is handled by a\n  different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"wood\", \"preservative\", \"chemical\", \"treatment\") can\naccidentally match inside the mock advisor's own default rationale\ntext for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy\npath -- this is exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a\ntreatment-facility coordination actor working adjacent to chemical\nwood-preservative work necessarily discusses those concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`woodtreatcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\ntreatment run\", \"finalize the treatment operation\", \"declare the\ntreated batch safe for handling\", \"override the shop safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`woodtreatcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for treater ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\ntreatment task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`woodtreatcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand its chemical-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override siblings\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7521\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7521`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 31 tests, 67 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-batch-clearance` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per\n  the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a chemical-safety-clearance\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision this severe (chemical-exposure/environmental-\n  handling risk from historically toxic wood-preservative compounds),\n  the capability itself must not exist. The only op related to\n  shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the\n  need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a treatment-execution or\n  chemical-safety-clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check used by some sibling actors):\n  rejected per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  preservative-chemicals/timber-stock order is not itself unsafe, so\n  it is handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  treatment-execution/chemical-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"wood\"\n  \"preservative\" \"chemical\"]`): rejected outright per the\n  fleet-known self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own\n  worked example for this exact task), and per the explicit\n  instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/\n  execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain\n  necessarily discusses wood/preservative/chemical/treatment/safety-\n  officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun\n  list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  (regression-tested directly against rationale text that deliberately\n  contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming only a single treatment-execution-finalization op family\n  (mirroring a narrower single-category exclusion shape used by some\n  sibling actors): rejected -- the task's domain design names two\n  distinct excluded decision categories (treatment-execution,\n  chemical-safety-clearance) plus a shop-safety-officer-judgment\n  override, so this ADR and the governor's\n  `scope-excluded-ops`/`scope-excluded-phrases` name both explicitly\n  (with handling AND shipment clearance variants for the\n  chemical-safety-clearance category, since a treated batch can be\n  declared safe for either purpose) rather than conflating them,\n  giving each its own dedicated unit test.\n- Merging `treater` and `facility` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered treater AND independently-registered\n  facility) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/facility\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered treater AND facility\n   (`:no-treater`/`:no-facility`). Not a treatment-execution or\n   chemical-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/treatment-cycle\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a treatment-execution or\n   chemical-safety-clearance decision (structurally absent from the\n   op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific treatment run or\n   batch clearance -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a chemical-exposure/\n   ventilation/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority, including\n   any chemical-safety-clearance decision.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- preservative-chemicals/\n   timber-stock procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a\n   treatment-execution, chemical-safety-clearance or authorization\n   decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated\n   by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na treatment-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nwood-treatment run), a chemical-safety-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring a treated batch safe for handling or shipment), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`woodtreatcoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) eleven\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`woodtreatcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`woodtreatcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-treatment-decision`\nand nine sibling tests), and (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check\nindependent of the `:op` field\n(`woodtreatcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a treatment run, finalize the treatment\noperation, declare a batch safe for handling or shipment, or override\na shop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`woodtreatcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-treatment-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-chemical-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-finalize-treatment-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 31, :assertions 67, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Wood Treatment Facility Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :treater-verification :facility-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7521", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7521], :test/simulator :woodtreatcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7521 — Wood Treaters Treatment-Facility Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7521}]
